php-vm calls proposal 0004: destructor and __clone visibility (zend_objects_destroy_object, ZEND_CLONE /
zend_bad_method_call). Applies after 0003. Files: exec.rs (call_destructor, new executed_scope helper),
props.rs (clone message).

- A private/protected destructor called while code is executing throws
  Error "Call to private X::__destruct() from scope Y|global scope". Private: the object's class must
  be zend_get_executed_scope(). Protected: zend_check_protected. With nothing executing (shutdown) it
  is skipped with Warning "Call to private X::__destruct() from global scope during shutdown ignored",
  reported at Unknown:0. The old `!in_shutdown` condition had both cases backwards.
  Fixes tests/classes/destructor_visibility_001, 002, factory_and_singleton_002, 005, 006, 009, 010.
- __clone visibility uses the master wording "Call to private method X::__clone() from global scope"
  (zend_bad_method_call, declaring class). Fixes tests/classes/factory_and_singleton_007, 008.
  (props.rs is outside the agreed call.rs/exec.rs scope: a one-line message change, take it or leave it.)

